WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.552
Visible values can be misleading.

00:00:02.552 --> 00:00:07.092
A column may contain digits but still be stored as text.

00:00:07.092 --> 00:00:11.027
A date may look like a date but still be a string.

00:00:11.027 --> 00:00:17.467
That is why we inspect data types and use the info function before doing calculations.

00:00:17.467 --> 00:00:23.232
In the example, order date and amount are initially stored as text.

00:00:23.232 --> 00:00:30.562
If amount remains text, mathematical operations may fail or produce unexpected behavior.

00:00:30.562 --> 00:00:38.283
If the date remains text, calendar operations such as extracting the month or weekday will not work correctly.

00:00:38.799 --> 00:00:41.986
Think of data types as part of data quality.

00:00:41.986 --> 00:00:48.223
Before asking what a column contains, also ask how Pandas is storing that column.
